# Project Requirements

## SQL Data Warehouse Project

| Category | Details |
|---|---|
| **Requested By** | Business Stakeholders |
| **Platform** | Microsoft SQL Server |
| **Teams** | Data Engineering & Data Analysis |

The project consists of two main phases: **Data Warehouse Development** and **Analytics & Reporting**. The first phase focuses on building a centralized data warehouse, while the second leverages the warehouse to generate business insights.

## 1. Building the Data Warehouse (Data Engineering)

### Objective
Develop a modern SQL Server-based data warehouse to consolidate sales data from multiple source systems, enabling analytical reporting and informed business decision-making.

### Specifications
- **Data Sources:** Import data from two source systems (ERP and CRM) provided in CSV format.
- **Data Quality:** Identify, cleanse, and resolve data quality issues before making the data available for analysis.
- **Data Integration:** Consolidate data from both source systems into a unified, user-friendly data model optimized for analytical queries.
- **Scope:** Focus on the latest available dataset. Historical data tracking (historization) is not required.
- **Documentation:** Maintain clear documentation of the data model to support business stakeholders and analytics teams.

## 2. BI — Analytics & Reporting (Data Analysis)

### Objective
Develop SQL-based analytics to generate meaningful business insights and support strategic decision-making.

### Analytical Focus Areas
- **Customer Behavior:** Analyze customer purchasing patterns, customer segmentation, and behavioral trends.
- **Product Performance:** Evaluate product sales, revenue contribution, and category performance.
- **Sales Trends:** Identify sales patterns, growth trends, and changes in business performance over time.

The resulting insights will provide stakeholders with key business metrics to support strategic planning and informed decision-making.

